         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the body is a company to which section 394 (duty to prepare individual company accounts) applies"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 394 (coa8)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
             IF `the Treasury has consented`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the consent of the Treasury"

-- src:20759 | (8) Whether or not the body is a company to which section 394 applies, the Secretary of State may direct that any provisions of this Act specified in the directions are to apply to the body, with or without any modifications so specified.
@ref sch 13 para 10(8) The Secretary of State may direct that provisions of this Act apply to an existing body (src:20759-20759)
GIVEN `the body is an existing body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 10(8) the Secretary of State may direct that provisions of this Act specified in the directions apply to the body` MEANS
    IF `the body is an existing body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "sub-paragraphs (7) and (8) apply only where the body is an existing body"

-- ---- paragraphs 11 to 13: supplementary provisions ----

-- src:20761 | 11 (1) The transfer of a function to a body designated by a delegation order does not affect anything previously done in the exercise of the function transferred; and the resumption of a function so transferred does not affect anything previously done in exercise of the function resumed.
@ref sch 13 para 11(1) The transfer or resumption of a function does not affect anything previously done (src:20761-20761)
GIVEN `the thing was done in the exercise of the function before it was transferred or resumed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 11(1) the transfer or resumption of the function affects the thing previously done` MEANS
    IF `the thing was done in the exercise of the function before it was transferred or resumed`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect anything previously done in the exercise of the function transferred"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything previously done in the exercise of the function"

-- src:20776 | 13 (1) This paragraph applies where the body is an unincorporated association.
-- src:20777 | (2) Any relevant proceedings may be brought by or against the body in the name of any body corporate whose constitution provides for the establishment of the body.
-- src:20778 | (3) In sub-paragraph (2) “relevant proceedings” means proceedings brought in or in connection with the exercise of any transferred function.
@ref sch 13 para 13(1)-(3) Proceedings by or against an unincorporated association in the name of a body corporate (src:20776-20778)
GIVEN `the body is an existing body that is an unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are brought in or in connection with the exercise of a transferred function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the body corporate provides for the establishment of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 para 13(2) the proceedings may be brought by or against the body in the name of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the body is an existing body that is an unincorporated association` AND `the proceedings are brought in or in connection with the exercise of a transferred function` AND `the constitution of the body corporate provides for the establishment of the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any relevant proceedings may be brought by or against the body in the name of any body corporate whose constitution provides for the establishment of the body"

